+
+### Bind real song assets (new)
+
+The optional **Song Reactive Landscape** sample now includes **Tools > DanceFlow >
+Samples > Create Source-Verified Song Profile...**. Import the exact original
+master into your project (prefer the original WAV for precise source frames),
+import a `dancerudiments.recording` using **Assets > DanceFlow**, and optionally
+attach the complete `stemlab.beat-timeline.v1` from the same source. The wizard
+hashes the actual master file and validates the timing map; per-song audio and
+recording data stay under **your** `Assets/`, never inside this UPM package.
+
+Select the generated SongShowcaseProfile asset and choose **Tools > DanceFlow >
+Samples > Create Scene From Selected Song Profile**. Playback keeps the actual
+song clock authoritative. Real recording playback requires a user-approved
+source-clock correspondence or an explicit musical retime. This cannot establish
+beat phase by guessing from a BPM hint. Star Lights Glow's *Mystery Liquid Kick*
+and *Anthem* remain independent profiles with no invented BPM.
+
+A standalone receipt tool can preflight local StemLab `.json` / `.json.gz`
+recordings and audio hashes before Unity import:
+
+```
+python tools~/showcase-checks/prepare_song_assets.py --song arcadians \
+  --master "../stemlab/examples/arcadians/Arcadians - 320kbps.mp3" \
+  --recording "./my-analysis/motion.json.gz" --bpm 145 \
+  --output "./local-assets/arcadians-receipt.json"
+```
+
+GPU recording shaders now support long captures using a **4 MiB maximum sliding
+window with one row of overlap**, not an unbounded upload or hidden truncation.
+The shader cursor uses the exact same signed source pip calculated by the CPU.
+GPU/Unity integration still requires running the licensed Unity test workflows;
+no claim of real hardware acceptance is made by standalone contract checks.
